    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nSuppose that we want to find an expression that is [MATH: 6] larger than the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (9-5) \\div 2]\n\nContent:\nLet's be careful of the language here. We want an expression that is \"[MATH: 6] larger\" than the one above, not \"[MATH: 6] times larger.\" Therefore, we should add [MATH: 6,] not multiply.\n\nContent:\nFirst, let's add some brackets:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: [(9-5) \\div 2]]\n\nContent:\nThen, we add [MATH: 6]:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 6+[(9-5) \\div 2]]\n\nContent:\nAnd we're done!\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Modifying an Expression With Addition\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat expression is [MATH: 3] larger than [MATH: 7 + (12\\div 2)?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, note that \"[MATH: {\\color{blue}3}] larger than\" means that we should add [MATH: 3] to the given expression.\n\nFirst, we add brackets:\n\n[MATH: [7 + (12\\div 2)]]\n\nNext, we add [MATH: \\color{blue}3]:\n\n[MATH: {\\color{blue}{3}}+[7 + (12\\div 2)]]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nWhich of the following is [MATH: 5] larger than the expression [MATH: 2 + (16 \u00f7 8)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 5 + [2 + (16 \u00f7 8)]]\nb. [MATH: 5 \u00f7 [2 + (16 \u00f7 8)]]\nc. [MATH: 5 \u2212 [2 + (16 \u00f7 8)]]\nd. [MATH: 5 \u00d7 [2 + (16 \u00f7 8)]]\ne. [MATH: [2 + (16 \u00f7 8)] \u00f7 5]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nWhich of the following is [MATH: 6] larger than the expression [MATH: 8 + (9 \u00f7 3)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [8 + (9 \u00f7 3)] \u00f7 6]\nb. [MATH: 6 \u2212 [8 + (9 \u00f7 3)]]\nc. [MATH: 6 + [8 + (9 \u00f7 3)]]\nd. [MATH: 6 \u00d7 [8 + (9 \u00f7 3)]]\ne. [MATH: 6 \u00f7 [8 + (9 \u00f7 3)]]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Tutorial: Modifying an Expression With Subtraction\n\nContent:\nSuppose that we want to find an expression that is [MATH: 8] smaller than the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (12+4) \\times 3]\n\nContent:\nLet's double-check the language that's used. We want an expression that is \"[MATH: 8] smaller\" than the one above. Therefore, we should subtract [MATH: 8.]\n\nContent:\nFirst, let's add some brackets:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: [(12+4) \\times 3]]\n\nContent:\nThen, we subtract [MATH: 8]:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: [(12+4) \\times 3] - 8]\n\nContent:\nAnd we're done!\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Example: Modifying an Expression With Subtraction\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind an expression that is [MATH: 4] smaller than the expression [MATH: 6 + (2\\times 9)?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, note that \"[MATH: {\\color{blue}4}] smaller than the expression\" means that we should subtract [MATH: 4] from the given expression.\n\nFirst, we add brackets:\n\n[MATH: [6 + (2\\times 9)]]\n\nNext, we subtract [MATH: \\color{blue}4]:\n\n[MATH: [6 + (2\\times 9)]-4]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nWhich of the following is [MATH: 7] smaller than the expression [MATH: 3 + (6 \u00d7 9)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: [3 + (6 \u00d7 9)] \u00f7 7]\nb. [MATH: [3 + (6 \u00d7 9)] \u2212 7]\nc. [MATH: [3 + (6 \u00d7 9)] + 7]\nd. [MATH: 7 \u00f7 [3 + (6 \u00d7 9)]]\ne. [MATH: [3 + (6 \u00d7 9)] \u00d7 7]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nWhich of the following is [MATH: 5] smaller than the expression [MATH: 9 \u00d7 (4 + 2)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 5 \u00d7 [9 \u00d7 (4 + 2)]]\nb. [MATH: [9 \u00d7 (4 + 2)] \u00f7 5]\nc. [MATH: 5 \u00f7 [9 \u00d7 (4 + 2)]]\nd. [MATH: 5 + [9 \u00d7 (4 + 2)]]\ne. [MATH: [9 \u00d7 (4 + 2)] \u2212 5]"
